id: pm-fud6qi
title: "Improvement-candidate synthesis: rank the next change to pm from evidence already recorded — recurrence, escape, blocked fan-out, cycle time and token cost — instead of from filing recency"
description: "Rank the next improvement from recorded recurrence, defect escape, blocked fan-out, cycle time, value, risk, and token cost rather than filing recency. Every recommendation must expose its evidence and counterfactuals, remain reproducible, and use bounded indexed computation across tiny and million-item workspaces."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-algorithms,ranking,self-improvement
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:09:44.534Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T14:36:34.141Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "A ranked candidate set is computed from tracked data alone and is reproducible from the same workspace state; Every candidate carries the evidence that produced its rank, so a human or agent can refute it; Ranking degrades sensibly from a few items to a million and never requires a full-corpus scan per query; The ranker is a declared member of the context algorithm portfolio rather than a private heuristic"
parent: pm-o0sqz5
risk: medium
confidence: medium
